form out?

Simone

---------- Forwarded message ----------
From: Corin Ilsley <corin.ilsley@corvane.example.test>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 07:31
Subject: Cross-Commodity Guarantee
To: simone.varga@corvane.example.test

Simone:

At long last I have had an opportunity to review the Multi-Purpose Form of
Guaranty you circulated in early October. I am fine with that form as somethi=
ng
that we can use and that Credit can send to counterparties.

As an aside, the attached e-mail indicates that you forwarded something
yesterday. If so, I did not see that.

I join in Tamsin's request to be forwarded a copy of the final form of
guarantee. Should you have any questions or comments, please contact me at
your convenience.

Corin

---------- Forwarded message ----------
From: Tamsin Ormsby <tamsin.ormsby@corvane.example.test>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 06:31
Subject: Cross-Commodity Guarantee
To: simone.varga@corvane.example.test

Simone:

As we discussed, Soren and I are fine with the Cross-Commodity Guarantee
you circulated yesterday. (By the way, we are revising our current physical
power guarantee to eliminate the 15-day cure period.) One question: Is CNA
the proper notice recipient in Section 7? We direct notice to Corvane Energy =
Inc. in
our standard form.

After you have received Lorcan's (et al.) feedback, please send me a copy of
the final form of cross-commodity guarantee so that we can include in our
form file for all requests.

Tamsin

